---
id: org.dxos.plugin.connector.events
name: Connector event dispatch
version: 0.1.0
---

Provider webhooks delivered to the spaces allowed to receive them: one Provider interface in place
of per-provider switches, an `event` trigger kind, routing on EDGE, and grants derived from OAuth
state. GitHub is the first provider.

This is part 3 of the GitHub sync design (see
[plugin-github/spec/SYNC.mdl](../../plugin-github/spec/SYNC.mdl)). It needs part 1's sync operation
to run; with it, part 1's poll becomes a slow backstop for missed deliveries. Nothing here is
GitHub-specific except `github.ts`.

It spans two repositories: `@dxos/compute` (the trigger kind) and plugin-connector live in
`dxos/dxos`; kms-service (which owns the Provider extension point and the webhook ingress) and
compute-service (which routes) live in `dxos/edge`.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `service`   | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`     |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`    |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`    |

