## Extension point

### `Provider` (kms-service)

An extension point of kms-service, not a separate package or worker. One module per external
service, registered in kms-service, so adding a provider is one module and its secrets, with no
`switch` to extend. Everything provider-specific (OAuth, tokens, access checks, webhook signatures)
stays in kms-service; compute-service only routes resource URIs and never sees a provider module.

```ts
// edge: packages/services/kms-service/src/providers/Provider.ts
import type * as Effect from 'effect/Effect';

import { type OAuthProvider } from '@dxos/protocols';

/** A resource an external service exposes, as host/path: `github.com/dxos/dxos`, `github.com/dxos`, `github.com`. */
export type ResourceUri = string & { readonly _ResourceUri: unique symbol };

/** One external service: how to authorize against it, check access on it, and receive its webhooks. */
export interface Provider {
  readonly id: OAuthProvider;
  /** Token-endpoint details; today's `AuthProviderData`, moved here unchanged. */
  readonly oauth: AuthProviderData;
  /** kms keeps the refresh token and hands the client a placeholder; required for `checkAccess`. */
  readonly managed: boolean;
  /** The account a token belongs to, recorded on the AccessToken. */
  account?(token: ProviderToken): Effect.Effect<ProviderAccount, ProviderError>;
  /** Whether the token's account may read `resource` now. */
  checkAccess?(token: ProviderToken, resource: ResourceUri): Effect.Effect<AccessVerdict, ProviderError>;
  /** Absent → the provider sends no webhooks and its bindings only poll. */
  readonly webhook?: ProviderWebhook;
}

export interface ProviderWebhook {
  /** Secret binding holding the provider's shared webhook secret, e.g. `GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET`. */
  readonly secret: string;
  /** Checks the request's signature (GitHub: `X-Hub-Signature-256`, HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body). */
  verify(request: Request, body: string, secret: string): Effect.Effect<boolean>;
  /** The provider's delivery id, for dedupe (GitHub: `X-GitHub-Delivery`). */
  deliveryId(request: Request): string;
  /** Parses a verified delivery. */
  parse(request: Request, body: string): Effect.Effect<ProviderEvent, ProviderError>;
  /** Resources the event concerns, most specific first: `github.com/dxos/dxos`, then `github.com/dxos`. */
  route(event: ProviderEvent): readonly ResourceUri[];
  /** Routes the event revokes (app uninstalled, authorization revoked); empty for ordinary events. */
  revokes(event: ProviderEvent): readonly Revocation[];
}

export type ProviderToken = { readonly accessToken: string; readonly account?: string };
export type ProviderAccount = { readonly id: string; readonly login: string };
export type AccessVerdict = { readonly allowed: boolean; readonly reason?: string };

export type ProviderEvent = {
  readonly provider: OAuthProvider;
  /** `pull_request`, `issues`, `push`, `check_suite`, … */
  readonly name: string;
  readonly action?: string;
  /** Provider-scoped installation id; GitHub sends `installation.id`. */
  readonly installation?: string;
  readonly payload: unknown;
};

export type Revocation =
  | { readonly kind: 'account'; readonly account: string }
  | { readonly kind: 'installation'; readonly installation: string }
  | { readonly kind: 'resource'; readonly resource: ResourceUri };

/** Every provider, keyed by id. kms-service's `getProviderData` switch becomes `Providers[id]`. */
export const Providers: Readonly<Partial<Record<OAuthProvider, Provider>>>;
```

```mdl
service Provider
  desc: kms-service's extension point for one external service. Implemented once per provider (github.ts, linear.ts, …); used by kms-service's OAuth flow, grant issuer and webhook ingress.
  ops:
    account(token: ProviderToken) → ProviderAccount
    checkAccess(token: ProviderToken, resource: ResourceUri) → AccessVerdict
    webhook.verify(request: Request, body: string, secret: string) → boolean
    webhook.deliveryId(request: Request) → string
    webhook.parse(request: Request, body: string) → ProviderEvent
    webhook.route(event: ProviderEvent) → ResourceUri[]
    webhook.revokes(event: ProviderEvent) → Revocation[]
  errors:
    ProviderError: the provider rejected the token or failed
```

GitHub's module, in outline:

```ts
// edge: packages/services/kms-service/src/providers/github.ts
export const GitHubProvider: Provider = {
  id: OAuthProvider.GITHUB,
  oauth: { /* today's getGitHubAuthProviderSpec() */ },
  managed: true,
  account: (token) => getJson('/user', token).pipe(Effect.map(({ id, login }) => ({ id: String(id), login }))),
  // github.com/<owner>/<repo> → GET /repos/<owner>/<repo>; github.com/<owner> and github.com → GET /user/installations.
  checkAccess: (token, resource) => ...,
  webhook: {
    secret: 'GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET',
    verify: (request, body, secret) => hmacSha256Equals(secret, body, request.headers.get('x-hub-signature-256')),
    deliveryId: (request) => request.headers.get('x-github-delivery') ?? '',
    parse: (request, body) => ...,
    // repository.full_name → github.com/<full_name>, then github.com/<owner>.
    route: (event) => ...,
    // github_app_authorization.revoked → account; installation.deleted → installation;
    // installation_repositories.removed → each removed repository.
    revokes: (event) => ...,
  },
};
```

### Connector declaration (`plugin-connector`)

A connector says which resource a binding listens to, so plugin-connector can create the event
trigger beside the timer trigger part 1 already creates.

```ts
// Added to ConnectorSpec.ConnectorSync (packages/plugins/plugin-connector/src/types/ConnectorSpec.ts).
/** Push events that re-run the sync for one binding; absent → the connector only polls. */
events?: {
  /** The resource a binding's events arrive for, e.g. `github.com/dxos/dxos` from the bound Repo. */
  resource: (binding: Cursor.ExternalCursor, target: Obj.Unknown) => string;
  /** Provider event names that wake the binding. */
  names: readonly string[];
};
```

## Types

### Trigger kind (`@dxos/compute`)

```ts
// packages/core/compute/compute/src/types/Trigger.ts — added to the Spec union.
/**
 * External event. Fires when a provider reports a change to `source` or anything below it.
 */
export const EventSpec = Schema.Struct({
  kind: Schema.Literal('event').annotate(kindLiteralAnnotations),
  /** Resource URI pattern: `github.com/dxos/dxos` (one repo), `github.com/dxos` (an org), `github.com` (everything the account sees). */
  source: Schema.String.annotate({ title: 'Source', examples: ['github.com/dxos/dxos'] }),
  /** Provider event names; omit for every event on the source. `issues.closed` narrows to one action. */
  events: Schema.optional(Schema.Array(Schema.String).annotate({ title: 'Events' })),
  /** The credential whose account access is checked against. */
  credential: Ref.Ref(AccessToken.AccessToken).annotate({ title: 'Credential' }),
  /** UCAN issued by EDGE after checking access; valid until `exp`. Written by EDGE, never by a user. */
  grant: Schema.optional(Schema.String.pipe(Annotation.FormInputAnnotation.set(false))),
});
export type EventSpec = Schema.Schema.Type<typeof EventSpec>;

export const specEvent = (opts: {
  source: string;
  credential: Ref.Ref<AccessToken.AccessToken>;
  events?: readonly string[];
}): EventSpec => ({ kind: 'event', ...opts });
```

```mdl
type EventSpec
  desc: Trigger spec kind `event` in @dxos/compute.
  fields:
    kind: event
    source: string                   # resource URI pattern
    events?: string[]                # provider event names, optionally `name.action`
    credential: Ref<AccessToken>
    grant?: string                   # UCAN, written by EDGE
```

### Grant

The grant caches one access check. It is a UCAN so the router can verify it without calling kms or
the provider on every delivery.

```ts
// UCAN 0.10 payload of an event grant.
type EventGrant = {
  /** EDGE's signing DID. */
  iss: string;
  /** The space's DID. */
  aud: string;
  att: [{ with: `dxos:event:${ResourceUri}`; can: 'event/subscribe' }];
  /** Issued-at + 24 hours. */
  exp: number;
  /** Binds the grant to the trigger and the token it was checked with. */
  fct: [{ spaceId: string; triggerId: string; accessTokenId: string; account: string }];
  prf: [];
};
```

```mdl
type EventGrant
  desc: UCAN issued by kms-service after Provider.checkAccess succeeds with the space's token.
  fields:
    iss: string                      # EDGE's DID
    aud: string                      # the space's DID
    with: string                     # dxos:event:<ResourceUri>
    can: event/subscribe
    exp: number                      # 24 hours after issue
    spaceId: string
    triggerId: string
    accessTokenId: string
    account: string                  # provider account the check ran as
```

### Routing (compute-service)

```ts
// edge: compute-service — one row per registered event trigger; D1 table `event_routes`.
type Route = {
  resource: ResourceUri;           // primary key part: the trigger's source
  spaceId: SpaceId;                // primary key part
  triggerId: ObjectId;             // primary key part
  provider: OAuthProvider;
  account: string;                 // for account revocations
  installation?: string;           // for installation revocations
  events?: readonly string[];
  grantExp: number;
};

/** What the TriggersDispatcher hands the trigger's runnable as `event.data`. Never the payload. */
type EventPoke = {
  provider: OAuthProvider;
  resource: ResourceUri;
  event: string;                   // `pull_request`
  action?: string;                 // `synchronize`
  deliveryId: string;
  receivedAt: string;
  /** Narrows the sync; the sync still reads everything with its own token. */
  hint?: { kind: 'pullRequest' | 'issue' | 'push' | 'checks'; number?: number; ref?: string };
};
```

```mdl
service EventRouter
  desc: Global index of event triggers in compute-service, keyed by resource.
  ops:
    register(trigger: EventSpec, spaceId: SpaceId, triggerId: ObjectId) → Route
    unregister(spaceId: SpaceId, triggerId: ObjectId) → void
    match(resources: ResourceUri[], event: ProviderEvent) → Route[]
    revoke(revocation: Revocation) → number
    dispatch(resources: ResourceUri[], event: ProviderEvent, deliveryId: string) → number   # called by kms-service's ingress; returns spaces poked
  errors:
    GrantInvalid: the grant's signature, audience, resource or expiry does not check out
```

```mdl
service EventGrants
  desc: Grant issuing in kms-service, which holds managed tokens.
  ops:
    issue(spaceId: SpaceId, triggerId: ObjectId, accessTokenId: string, source: ResourceUri) → string
  errors:
    NotManaged: the credential's provider keeps its token on the client, so kms cannot check access
    AccessDenied: Provider.checkAccess refused the resource
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Provider registry

  req F-1.1: Every provider is one module implementing Provider, registered in kms-service; kms-service looks providers up in Providers and contains no per-provider branch, and compute-service contains no provider code at all.

  req F-1.2: kms-service's OAuth flow reads `Providers[id].oauth`; today's AuthProviderData moves without change.

  req F-1.3: GitHub is a managed provider: kms keeps its refresh token, and the client's AccessToken holds the placeholder, as Google's does today.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Event trigger and grant

  req F-2.1:
    when: a connector with `events` binds a target
    then: plugin-connector creates an event trigger with source = events.resource(binding), credential = the connection's AccessToken, and remote = true, running the connector's sync operation

  req F-2.2:
    when: compute-service loads an event trigger without a valid grant
    then: it calls EventGrants.issue; on success it writes the grant to the trigger and registers the route

  req F-2.4: Access is never inferred from the trigger alone; it comes from Provider.checkAccess with the space's own managed token.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Ingress

  req F-3.1: One endpoint per provider, `POST /events/<provider id>`, served by kms-service, which holds the webhook secrets; after verify, dedupe, parse and route it calls EventRouter.dispatch over its service binding to compute-service.

  req F-3.2:
    when: a delivery arrives
    then: it is verified with Provider.webhook.verify before parsing; an unverified delivery answers 401 and is not logged beyond its delivery id

  req F-3.3: A delivery id seen in the last 24 hours is answered 200 and dropped.

  req F-3.4: The ingress answers within 1 second and fans out from a queue, because GitHub times out slow receivers.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Routing and delivery

  req F-4.1: A route matches when its resource is one of Provider.webhook.route(event) and its events, if set, include the event name or name.action.

  req F-4.2: A match is delivered to the space's TriggersDispatcher as an EventPoke; the provider's payload never enters a space.

  req F-4.3: Deliveries to one trigger are coalesced for 5 seconds, so a burst of events runs the sync once.

  req F-4.4: The router checks grantExp on delivery and drops routes past it.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Revocation

  req F-5.1:
    when: Provider.webhook.revokes returns revocations
    then: EventRouter.revoke removes every matching route

  req F-5.2:
    when: kms deletes a managed token
    then: every route registered with that token's account is removed

  req F-5.3:
    when: an event trigger is deleted or disabled
    then: its route is removed on the dispatcher's next load
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Backstop

  req F-6.1: While a binding's event trigger holds a valid grant, plugin-connector sets the binding's timer trigger to an hourly schedule, and restores the 3-minute default when the grant lapses. The schedule lives only on the trigger.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Push to a bound repository
  given: a space bound to dxos/dxos with a valid event grant
  when: GitHub delivers pull_request.synchronize for dxos/dxos#12
  then:
    - the delivery verifies and routes to github.com/dxos/dxos
    - the space receives one EventPoke with hint { kind: pullRequest, number: 12 }
    - part 1's sync runs and updates PullRequest #12
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Unauthorized space
  given: a space whose account cannot read acme/secret
  when: it creates an event trigger with source github.com/acme/secret
  then:
    - EventGrants.issue fails with AccessDenied
    - no route exists for that trigger and the trigger's lastError names the refusal
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Forged delivery
  given: a request to /events/github whose signature does not match the body
  when: it arrives
  then:
    - the ingress answers 401
    - no route is matched and no space is poked
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: App uninstalled
  given: routes registered for installation 42
  when: GitHub delivers installation.deleted for installation 42
  then:
    - every route with installation 42 is removed
    - the affected bindings fall back to part 1's poll interval
```

## Open questions

1. One GitHub App per environment, or one App whose endpoint forwards by environment.
2. Whether `github.com/<owner>` and `github.com` patterns should be allowed: they route by installation, so a space can learn that a repository it cannot read changed, though never what changed.
3. Which existing DXOS key signs grants as EDGE, and the space's DID format; `@dxos/permission` mentions UCAN and should be checked first.

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Part 3 of the GitHub sync design is webhook dispatch: an event trigger type, routing, and permissions.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BvVEssur2xxCiXewKjKQ3Z
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The new trigger type is `event`. Its source is a URI or pattern for a resource, such as `github.com` or `github.com/dxos/dxos`. EDGE gives the space a credential, a UCAN, that shows the space can actually access those events.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [EventSpec, EventGrant, F-2]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BvVEssur2xxCiXewKjKQ3Z
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Access may need no separate credential and may be inferred from OAuth state instead.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.4]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BvVEssur2xxCiXewKjKQ3Z
```

```mdl
decision D-4: A wide Provider (service) interface replaces the switch over providers.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [Provider, F-1]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BvVEssur2xxCiXewKjKQ3Z
```

```mdl
decision D-5: Access is checked from OAuth state, which requires GitHub to become a managed provider; the UCAN of [D-2] caches that check for 24 hours, so the router verifies it without calling kms or GitHub per delivery. Fills in [D-2] and [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.3, F-2, EventGrant]
  why: Only a token held on EDGE can prove access to EDGE without sending it; a grant with expiry gives revocation a bound and keeps per-event cost at a signature check.
  rejected:
    - Check access with the provider on every delivery: one provider request per event per space.
    - UCAN without managed tokens: nothing on EDGE could check the claim before signing it.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The Provider interface carries OAuth data, account, checkAccess and an optional webhook part (verify, deliveryId, parse, route, revokes), in a new edge package shared by kms-service and compute-service. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [Provider, F-1, F-3]
  rejected:
    - A separate github-service worker: the only GitHub-specific code is the module itself.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: A delivery is a poke: the payload never enters a space, and the space's sync reads what changed with its own token. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [EventPoke, F-4.2]
  why: A routing mistake then cannot leak content, at the cost of one read per event.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Routes live in a global D1 table in compute-service, ingress is `POST /events/<provider>`, and deliveries to one trigger coalesce for 5 seconds. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [EventRouter, F-3, F-4]
  why: Each space's TriggersDispatcher sees only its own space, so the reverse index from resource to spaces must be global.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: The Provider interface is not a new edge service or package; it is an extensibility point in kms-service.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [Provider, F-1]
  supersedes: D-6
  source: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BvVEssur2xxCiXewKjKQ3Z
```

```mdl
decision D-10: kms-service also serves the webhook ingress and calls compute-service's EventRouter.dispatch with the routed resources; compute-service has no provider code. Fills in [D-9].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.1, EventRouter, F-1.1]
  why: Verifying a webhook needs the provider module and its secret, both of which now live only in kms-service; routing by resource URI stays generic.
  rejected:
    - Ingress in compute-service calling kms-service per delivery to verify: one extra service-binding hop per event and webhook secrets readable outside kms.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: The spec omits renewing a grant before it expires (formerly F-2.3).
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2, EventSpec]
  source: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/3c2feabe-985f-479a-aeea-1d598f6bf1e0
```

```mdl
decision D-12: The connector declares no backstop interval; while events flow, plugin-connector edits the timer trigger's own schedule, so the interval lives only on the trigger. Follows from plugin-github SYNC.mdl D-7.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6.1]
  why: A backstop interval on the connector would mirror the trigger's schedule, which SYNC.mdl D-7 rules out.
```
